cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository in research, teaching, or diligence, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Delayed Divergence: A Reproducible Evidence Audit of the Moderna-Merck mRNA Melanoma Vaccine and Its Market Reaction"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Delayed Divergence contributors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A clean-room, reproducible evidence audit of the Moderna-Merck individualized
  mRNA melanoma vaccine (intismeran autogene, V940/mRNA-4157). The repository
  grades 42 claims against 29 sources, reconstructs the Phase 3 clinical result,
  estimates market-model abnormal returns with placebo inference, and provides
  an offline Python pipeline, committed source snapshots, SHA-256 manifests,
  tests, and an interactive static preview.
keywords:
  - evidence audit
  - reproducible research
  - mRNA cancer vaccine
  - intismeran autogene
  - melanoma
  - event study
  - claim verification
  - open source
